// `for ... between (x0, y0) and (x1, y1) in Index` against a scan of all:
// every dot's count of the dots in a box around it, and the sum of where
// they are seen. In a box that wraps (each seen at its image from the
// lowest corner on: never outside the corners), across its edges, a
// whole number of boxes away, and almost or quite as wide as it; in a
// grid of whole numbers over where the dots are, past its edge and with
// the corners the wrong way round (by blocks of rows, as the statements
// write). The same on one core and on all.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/between.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/between.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRAP --input-file=%t.one
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/between_whole_wrap.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.ww
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/between_whole_wrap.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.ww.all
// RUN: cmp %t.ww %t.ww.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLEWRAP --input-file=%t.ww
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/between_whole.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.open
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/between_whole.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.open.all
// RUN: cmp %t.open %t.open.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OPEN --input-file=%t.open
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/between_whole.ent -I %S/../../devices \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR

